/*  How many phases? -- water / 1-butanol at 298.15 K, the tangent plane.

    The same system and the same cited UNIQUAC set as binary01, with the
    optional `stability` block of propertyScanBinary switched on: besides
    g_mix and the two coexisting liquids, the activities of both components
    on a 100-node grid, the activities in the two liquids, the tangent-plane
    distance of the declared feed (z(water) = 0.80, inside the gap) and the
    verdict of the engine's own Michelsen test on it.  The golden pins that
    verdict and its distances.  See README.md. */
application   choupoProps;
description   "How many phases? Water + 1-butanol at 298.15 K: g_mix, activities and the Michelsen tangent-plane distance via propertyScanBinary (stability block), cited Winkelman 2009 UNIQUAC";
verbosity     2;
